--- !u!114 &442153283
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 442153279}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 0
  fontSize: 8
  pages:
  - "Excerpt from the Gravekeeper\u2019s Notes\nAnderson family\n\nThere is only
    one grave under the Anderson name.\n\nAnthony Anderson\u2019s burial was arranged
    quickly. The paperwork was submitted by different hands and corrected more than
    once, as though responsibility had been passed around before settling where it
    could. No one stayed long enough to be counted.\n\nHe was a father of three.
    None of them attended. This was explained as practical. Children, I was told,
    should not be exposed to unnecessary scenes."
  - "Little was said of Anthony\u2019s life. When it was mentioned, it was done cautiously,
    with emphasis on what he had insisted upon rather than what he had achieved.
    He was described as difficult, then later as uncompromising, and finally not
    described at all.\n\nIn the months before his death, he had been seen often and
    then not at all. Certain doors stopped opening to him. This was never framed
    as exclusion, only as circumstance."
  - 'His death was recorded as sudden. The timing suggested otherwise.


    No items
    have appeared at his grave. Even so, the ground settles unevenly there, as if
    pressed by weight that did not belong to the soil alone.


    I have been asked
    whether the children will be buried nearby in time. I have not been instructed
    to answer.'
