--- !u!114 &681295816
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 681295812}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 0
  fontSize: 8
  pages:
  - "Excerpt from the Gravekeeper\u2019s Notes\nHolmes family\n\nThere are two graves
    under the Holmes name.\n\nThey were prepared together. The paperwork was submitted
    by a third party and completed without error. No revisions were requested. The
    plots were placed side by side, close enough that the soil between them had to
    be reinforced. This was described as practical.\n\nThe deceased are Edward Holmes
    and Zackary Holmes. Edward was young. Zackary was his father. The age difference
    was noted only once, when confirming the order of burial. No preference was expressed.\n\nThey
    were brought to the grounds on the same morning. No service was held. I was told
    that any gathering would complicate matters. When I asked whether other family
    would attend, I was informed that Zackary had a brother, but that he would not
    be coming. No explanation followed."
  - 'What is known of the incident is limited and consistent. The two were found
    together, some distance from town, in a place not intended for long stays. It
    was said they had gone there deliberately, though for what purpose was never
    clarified. Circumstances suggested preparation. Circumstances also suggested
    delay.


    In the weeks prior, the Holmes household had become difficult to
    place. Neighbors reported seeing lights at odd hours, then not seeing them at
    all. Deliveries were left longer than usual before being collected. Questions
    were asked, then stopped. Whether this was discretion or disinterest, I cannot
    say.


    Zackary Holmes had once been considered reliable. Edward was described
    as well liked. These descriptions were offered carefully, as though no longer
    current. When the deaths were discussed, the language shifted to inevitability.
    People spoke of distance, of misunderstandings, of how things had become complicated.
    No one spoke of intervention.'
  - 'No objects have appeared at either grave. The ground remains undisturbed. It
    is as though the matter concluded itself.


    The brother has not come. I was
    told he had been advised against it, for his own sake.


    Edward and Zackary
    Holmes rest side by side. The space around them is neat, orderly, and avoided.


    There
    is nothing outwardly remarkable about this. That, too, has been remarked upon.'
--- !u!64 &681295817
