--- !u!114 &815585405
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 815585402}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 272
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 0
  fontSize: 8
  pages:
  - "Excerpt from the Gravekeeper\u2019s Notes\nHuang family\n\nThere is only one
    grave under the Huang name.\n\nThis is unusual, given the care taken in its placement.
    The plot was chosen by Huang Wenqi himself. He arrived with the paperwork already
    prepared, spoke clearly, and did not linger. Men who do this are not unfamiliar
    with loss; they are rehearsed. He asked about soil depth and drainage, not about
    prayers.\n\nThe deceased is Madam Huang. She was brought to the grounds at dawn.
    No extended family accompanied the body. Only the husband signed the ledger.
    When I asked whether the son would attend the burial, Wenqi said the family was
    complete as it stood. He did not look at the coffin when he said this.\n\nNo
    further details were requested."
  - "Mei Huang had lived quietly, yet her presence was felt in small ways: neighbors
    received meals she prepared, stray animals were sheltered under her care, and
    children in the eastern quarter were tended when others could not. Her deeds
    were rarely spoken of and, over time, fewer people noticed at all. By the final
    months, even those who had once counted on her assistance had stopped seeking
    her out. I do not know whether this absence of attention was intentional, or
    simply the way the world turned, but the quiet left her more vulnerable than
    it should have.\n\nAs for the boy\u2019s dishonor, I was given no explanation.
    The word was used once and never repeated. It was said the matter was finished,
    yet the family continues to arrange itself around it, as one arranges furniture
    around a locked door."
  - "No offerings are made in the son\u2019s name. None are permitted. Still, certain
    items have appeared near the grave that were not placed there by the groundskeepers:
    a folded paper charm without writing, a child\u2019s coin worn smooth, once a
    length of red thread cut cleanly at both ends. I remove these when I find them.
    They return regardless.\n\nHuang Wenqi comes alone now. He does not stay long.
    Before leaving, he always checks the stone for damage, as if expecting it to
    change while he is gone.\n\nThere is room beside Madam Huang\u2019s grave for
    another coffin. I have been instructed to keep it unassigned.\n\nNo reason was
    given."
--- !u!23 &815585406
