--- !u!114 &862539189
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 862539186}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 0
  fontSize: 8
  pages:
  - "Excerpt from the Gravekeeper\u2019s Notes\nAdams family\n\nThere is only one
    grave under the Adams name.\n\nThe burial was arranged by extended family. The
    paperwork arrived in stages, amended more than once before it was finalized.
    No one claimed responsibility for the delays.\n\nThe deceased is Jane Adams.\n\nShe
    was brought to the grounds in the early morning. No public notice was posted.
    A small group stood at a distance during the service, close enough to be counted,
    far enough to avoid conversation. When I asked whether her son would attend,
    I was told he had been sent elsewhere for the time being. This was said as a
    kindness."
  - 'Jane Adams had been well known once. Her name appeared often in correspondence,
    on guest lists, in shared records that implied trust and familiarity. In the
    final years, it appeared less. Not because she withdrew entirely, but because
    others learned to speak around her. Invitations stopped being extended. Conversations
    ended when she entered a room. I noted this only because it happened gradually,
    and then all at once.


    No explanation was offered for the change. None was
    required.'
  - 'In the weeks before her death, arrangements were made quietly. Personal effects
    were sorted earlier than necessary. Certain matters were settled in advance,
    as though continuation was no longer assumed. When the end came, it was described
    as sudden. The signs suggested otherwise.


    There were no offerings placed
    at her grave. Still, the soil has been disturbed more than once, shallow marks
    that suggest hesitation rather than maintenance. I smooth them out when I notice.
    They return irregularly.


    Her son has not come. I am told he asks questions.
    I am also told it is better that he not receive answers yet.


    Jane Adams
    rests here alone. Those who once called her a friend do not visit. Those who
    remain speak of her softly, if at all, and only after ensuring no one else is
    listening.


    There is nothing unusual about this arrangement. I have seen
    it before.'
--- !u!23 &862539190
