  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: af6c11f0d531f4249801ea5c2de41bcb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ReadableTrigger
  interactionPrompt: Read
  backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5face2da520a6fa4fa8eff1c614aff70, type: 3}
  fontOverride: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4cf2c21c93fda745b09b91b791a22c2, type: 2}
  overrideAlignment: 0
  textAlignment: 257
  overrideMargins: 0
  textMargins: {x: 30, y: 30, z: 0, w: 0}
  overrideLineSpacing: 0
  lineSpacing: 0
  overrideFontSize: 1
  fontSize: 18
  pages:
  - 'The Watchman''s Notes

    1999'
  - In this book you will find instructions on how to watch over this graveyard.
    It is important that you do not deviate from these instructions. This book contains
    a compilation of all recordings from previous grave watchers.
  - As the gravekeeper, the most important rule is to respect the dead. This eternal
    resting place is centuries old and must not be tampered with. You will not allow
    any visitors that will disturb the gravesites.
  - You must not allow anyone who is not directly related to the deceased to visit
    any gravesites. Friends, accomplices, or anyone who is not directly related to
    the dead should be turned away.
  - You must periodically patrol the graveyard to ensure the integrity of the gravesites.
    You must also stand guard at the gate to prevent unwanted visitors from tampering
    with the gravesites.
  - Ensure that the cabin and the lanterns near the cabin and crypt are lit at all
    times. Do not shine your flashlight on tombstones.
  - Ensure that the crucifix is affixed to the door of the cabin at all times.
  - Do not blindly trust visitors. Always cross reference any information they provide
    you.
--- !u!64 &1217414737
